infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Referral vs authoritative answer
  desc Two response shapes — which DNS message sections each fills, and the AA bit
  compares
    - label Referral (root, TLD)
      children
        - label Answer section empty
          desc Server does not own the name, so it answers nothing directly
        - label NS in Authority
          desc Nameserver for the next zone down the tree
        - label Glue A/AAAA in Additional
          desc Pre-fetched IP of that nameserver, so no lookup loop
        - label AA bit = 0
          desc Not an authoritative answer — just a pointer onward
    - label Authoritative answer
      children
        - label Answer section populated
          desc e.g. cdn.example.co.uk A 203.0.113.10 TTL=300
        - label Authority optional
          desc May echo the zone's own NS records
        - label Additional often empty
          desc No referral target to glue — this is the final hop
        - label AA bit = 1
          desc Responding server owns the zone
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
